# Ultimate Fun Zone

An Android starter game project for Ultimate Fun Zone.

## Included
- Android app shell using a built-in WebView (no third-party Android libraries).
- Offline pass-and-play for 2–4 players and solo practice.
- Easy, medium and hard arithmetic, rounding, place-value and time-rounding questions.
- Timed multiple-choice turns and local score tracking.
- GitHub Actions workflow to build a debug APK.

## Build an APK on GitHub
1. Create a GitHub repository named `ultimate-fun-zone`.
2. Upload the **contents** of this project folder (not the ZIP file itself) to the repository root.
3. Open the repository's **Actions** tab and enable Actions if prompted.
4. Run the workflow named **Build Android APK**, or push a commit to `main`.
5. Open the completed workflow run, scroll to **Artifacts**, and download `UltimateFunZone-debug-apk`.
6. Extract the downloaded artifact ZIP on your Android phone and install the APK. Android may ask you to allow installs from your browser/files app.

## Online multiplayer
The Online option is intentionally marked as requiring a server. A secure online mode needs a backend for room creation, player identity, synchronized turns and score validation. Do not expose private server credentials in the app. This starter does not claim online play is already implemented.

## Project details
- Package: `com.hollyfurniture.ultimatefunzone`
- Minimum Android version: Android 6.0 (API 23)
- App version: 1.0
